WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.314
This is the executive
briefing for Book 00 of the

2
00:00:03.314 --> 00:00:07.313
Federal Modernization Workbook,
Orientation and Program.

3
00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:12.097
It runs about thirty minutes, and it's
for the people who sponsor, fund and

4
00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:17.612
answer for modernization: executive
sponsors, CIOs, CISOs and program executives.

5
00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:18.825
One point first.

6
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:23.062
The workbook is independent technical
guidance, not federal policy.

7
00:00:23.062 --> 00:00:25.826
Where it says a law,
memorandum or directive

8
00:00:25.826 --> 00:00:28.437
requires something, it cites that source.

9
00:00:28.437 --> 00:00:31.986
Everything else, including
the program's phases, gates,

10
00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:36.558
principles and decision rights, is
the workbook's own recommendation:

11
00:00:36.558 --> 00:00:40.500
one way to meet those requirements,
not a requirement itself.

12
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.925
The argument is short.

13
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:46.462
For twenty years Active Directory
quietly did governance nobody wrote down.

14
00:00:46.462 --> 00:00:51.612
Federal policy and vendor lifecycles
now set clocks the estate can't ignore.

15
00:00:51.612 --> 00:00:56.950
Meeting them one product at a time rebuilds
the same governance gaps in a new place,

16
00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.325
so modernization has to run
as one governed program.

17
00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:04.265
I'll take four questions in order:
why now, what the program is,

18
00:01:04.265 --> 00:01:08.125
who decides, and how it runs
from pre-flight to steady state.

19
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:12.740
Every decision slide names the decision,
its owner, and when it's needed.
